1790632593125977	agentbus-8lbb0p	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2m4	{"description":"prime_stream (src/main.rs) reads the saved prefix with BufReader::read_line into a String. read_line returns InvalidData on a line with invalid UTF-8, and priming returns early, so parser state after that line is never rebuilt (e.g. the last Claude answer carried into a later turn_end). The live tail path decodes such lines lossily since bn-1q3, so the two paths now disagree.\n\nFix: read_until(b'\\n') into a Vec<u8> and decode each complete line lossily, matching tail::poll. Keep the existing rule that a trailing partial line is not fed to the parser. Regression test: a prefix containing an invalid byte on one line followed by a session line must still prime the later line. Found by the bn-1q3 agent; confirmed in review.","kind":"bug","labels":["verification"],"parent":"bn-3v2","size":"xs","title":"Stream priming stops at the first line that is not valid UTF-8"}	blake3:yB_hr_TjinyZvubhb0BLvMv9SAQUGQZcFZLJhJ0dGEo
1790632593224116	agentbus-8lbb0p	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2hu	{"description":"From the bn-38j baseline, the misses not covered by bn-3s2/bn-wo6:\n- completion::clamp_result and MAX_RESULT_BYTES: no test. Needs: a result_full over 1 MiB is clamped, cut on a char boundary (multibyte at the cut), marked result_truncated, and one at exactly the limit is untouched.\n- tail: poll after the file is truncated (jumps to the new end, clears partial, replays nothing), reset_to_end, is_tracked, checkpoints contents.\n- wait: the blocked exit path (snapshot says blocked -> exit 3 with detail), --json output shape, result_of preferring result_full over result, --pid/--cwd parsing.\nPlain unit tests are the right tool here; no property needed. Blocks the final rerun (bn-33u).","kind":"task","labels":["verification"],"parent":"bn-3v2","size":"s","title":"Close untested surfaces the mutants baseline exposed"}	blake3:bFuEw__uJSKfqDLIGuj6rldi7Dn5wmcPdIkXXQWCVh8
1790632593246168	agentbus-8lbb0p	itc:AQ		item.link	bn-33u	{"link_type":"blocks","target":"bn-2m4"}	blake3:UgYu5gbgSoIgsvPaAC6wGi0Mr5Va0JsmUhBROpoXvWM
1790632593262223	agentbus-8lbb0p	itc:AQ		item.link	bn-33u	{"link_type":"blocks","target":"bn-2hu"}	blake3:w0--_Kj7iYjF3fbji6EbPXzYpuWmAZSRBGqlbP_dKsY
1790632603742849	agentbus-8lbb0p	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-38j	{"body":"Baseline at 4e80d67 (before any bn-3v2 fixes): 123 mutants in 4m; 49 caught, 47 missed, 22 timeouts, 5 unviable. Timeouts are wait-loop mutants that hang the wait tests; treated as caught.\n\nMissed, by area:\n- completion newest_since expiry condition (lines 147, 153; 10 mutants): the bn-3s2 bug lives here. Covered by bn-3s2 and bn-wo6.\n- completion prune boundaries (186 age cutoff < vs <=, 193 record/byte caps; 7): off-by-one at every retention limit is untested. bn-wo6 should close these.\n- completion clamp_result and MAX_RESULT_BYTES (13, 218-229; 7): the 1 MiB result clamp has no test at all. Filed as part of bn-2hu.\n- completion now_epoch (238; 2): wall-clock, justified as untestable.\n- tail is_tracked, checkpoints, reset_to_end, poll truncation branch (57, 70, 87, 120, 136; 7): no test truncates a followed file or resets a cursor. 120 and 136 '<'->'<=' look equivalent (len==offset returns early; the read loop stops at EOF). bn-2hu.\n- wait CLI surface (parse arms for --pid/--cwd/--json, result_of, Outcome::code/print, state_of; 14): the blocked exit path and output formatting are untested. bn-2hu."}	blake3:sV9XYxlkb_iYM1fknhsKHjJB-NyiK3Kt-_sNPg-5_Co
